Task: Linter and formatter configuration (Phase 1, Track foundation-core_20260918)

What was done:
- Declared the application's injected globals as read-only for the linter, plus
  the two entry-point names it looks up by name in our own code.
- Set the line width and indentation to match the project's style guide.
- Kept the table-call idiom by configuring the formatter not to add parentheses
  around a single table argument.
- Formatted the existing source and confirmed both tools report clean.

Findings worth keeping:
- The package manager installs command-line tools into a user-local directory
  that is not on the default non-interactive path; the setup notes already say
  to add it, and any automated run must do so explicitly.
- The formatter insists on a space between a call and its table argument, and
  the option that looks like it would suppress that does not. The formatter's
  preference was accepted rather than worked around, and the ineffective option
  was removed instead of being left in the configuration as dead weight.

Files changed:
- .luacheckrc, stylua.toml, main.lua (reformatted)

Why:
The quality gates in the process document name lint and format cleanliness as
conditions for completing any task. Without configuration matching the
application's runtime, the linter would have reported every API call as an
error and the gate would have been ignored in practice.
